<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Javols</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Anderitum</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Javols is a village in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lozere">Lozère</a> in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, on the site of Anderitum, the chief town of the Gabali under Roman rule. Excavations have revealed a forum, baths and other remains of the Roman town. The seat of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> of the Gabali was later moved from there to Mende, which became the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gevaudan">Gévaudan</a>.</p></div>
